  "@id": "https://w3id.org/pices/odis/records/zenodo-23605449.jsonld",
  "@type": "Dataset",
  "name": "Prince William Sound Nowcast-Forecast System (PWS NFS)",
  "description": "The PWS NFS has both modeling and observational components, and utilizes both new and existing monitoring sites. The observational network includes 2 NDBC buoys, 3 NDBC C-MAN stations, 3 NOS tide gauge stations, 3 hydrographic stations, ADCP transects, satellite-tracked drifting buoys, and a GEM-EVOS sponsored ADCP mooring at Hinchinbrook Entrance. The observational network has recently been expanded to include 4 more meteorological stations. Additionally, sampling of nekton and plankton is carried out at various sites throughout the sound. Archived and near real-time data and model simulations will soon be publicly available on a web site. Observations include water temperature, salinity, water level, tides, currents, plankton and nekton net surveys, wind speed/direction/gust, atmospheric pressure, air temperature, and dew point.\n\nDeposited content: descriptive metadata only; underlying research data are not included.",
